# Web SEO: Blog post body (CMS HTML)

Public posts at `/blog/[slug]` render CMS HTML through `BlogPost.svelte` after `normalizeBlogContentLinks`. Edit in secret-admin **HTML source** (or visual) — do not add a markdown file under `web/src/content` for blog articles.

FAQ, HowTo, Product, and optional **Audience card** blocks are **form fields** (`faq_items`, `howto_name`, `howto_steps`, `product`, `audience_card`). They render in `BlogPostSeoBlocks` (audience card has no section title—one compact card) and JSON-LD (`createBlogPostSEOSchema` + `createPublicAudienceSectionSEOSchema` for `#audience`). Do not duplicate those Q&A / step lists as a second accordion in `content`.

**How-to title** (`howto_name`) is optional plain text. When set, it is the on-page step-summary heading and `HowTo.name` in JSON-LD; when empty, both fall back to the post title.

**Feature Walkthroughs by Use Case** (`feature-walkthroughs-by-use-case`) emit `BlogPosting` + `Guide` on the same JSON-LD node via `createBlogPostSEOSchema` — including optional `about` as `SoftwareApplication` — with **no extra admin form fields**. Editors only need the correct topic; do not add a Guide block to `content` or structured SEO fields.

**How-to steps and product summary** are **optional on every blog topic** (including Educational Guides). The blog manager shows those fields whenever a topic is selected; JSON-LD and `BlogPostSeoBlocks` render them when filled in. **Product summary is never auto-filled** from the post title or description—leave it empty unless you intentionally want Product JSON-LD.

**FAQ answers and How-to step text** use the same Visual / HTML source editor as Content (`BlogRichTextField`). Questions and step **names** stay plain text. Paste root-relative `<a href="/tools/skill-builder">Skill Builder</a>` (or use Visual → link; the prompt keeps `/…` paths). Visible HTML is normalized with `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay`; JSON-LD `Answer.text` / `HowToStep.text` is **plain text** (`stripHtmlToPlainText`) so schema stays valid.

## Audience card (`audience_card`)

Optional **admin form block** (unlocked after **Topic** is selected). Renders **below the hero** as one compact card (“This blog is for …”). Emits `Audience` JSON-LD via `createPublicAudienceSectionSEOSchema` (`#blog-post-audience`). **Do not** repeat the same persona paragraph in `content` HTML.

| Field | Format | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **preset** | One of `developer`, `team-social-managers`, `founders`, `marketers`, `self-host-operators`, `custom` | Chooses preset icon and colors (`blogAudienceCardPresets.ts`) |
| **title** | Plain text (card headline) | Shown after “This blog is for” — keep short (e.g. `Founders shipping with Grok Bot`) |
| **description** | Plain text | 1–3 ASD-STE100 sentences: who should read and why **this** post |
| **audience_type** | Optional plain text | Schema.org `audienceType`; when empty, JSON-LD falls back to **title** |

**When to fill it in**

- How-to tutorials, educational guides, and long agent/skill posts with a clear reader (founders, social leads, developers).
- Competitive or keyword posts where persona clarity helps CTR—without pasting a second “who is this for” section in the body.

**Handoffs and AI copy-paste packs** (`docs/blog/*-blog-manager-copy-paste.md`) must include an **Audience card** section with all four fields so operators do not skip the block.

Presets are a starting point only—**edit title and description** to match the article; use `custom` when no preset fits.

## Pick the tool page, not the hub

Do **not** send most equity to `/tools`. Link the **specific** tool the article is about.

| Article topic | Primary href | Typical anchors |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Agent skills, `SKILL.md`, zips, CLI recipes, Codex/ChatGPT skills | `/tools/skill-builder` | Skill Builder |
| Same + a named channel | `/tools/skill-builder/{slug}` | TikTok Skill Builder |
| Timing tests / “when to post” (secondary unless the post is about timing) | `/tools/best-time-to-post` or `…/{slug}` | Best Time to Post calculator |
| Stills / covers / aspect ratios | `/tools/photo-editor` or `…/{slug}` | Photo Editor |
| Humanizer / “sound more human” / less machine-written drafts | `/tools/humanizer` or `…/{slug}` | Humanizer |
| Listing several unrelated utilities | `/tools` (at most once) | OpenQuok free tools |

Skills / MCP / CLI how-tos (ChatGPT, Codex, OpenClaw, CapCut + OpenQuok Core) → **Skill Builder is the primary internal tool link**. Mention `/tools` only if you truly mean the whole catalog.

Prefer **one or two** links per destination. Repeat the tool name in prose without linking every mention.

## Agent chat prompts and paste blocks in `content`

Match the UX of agent posts such as [Schedule Social Posts from Grok Bot with OpenQuok](/blog/schedule-social-posts-from-grok-bot-with-openquok) and MCP docs (`> List my connected social media accounts.` as rendered from blockquotes).

| Kind | HTML pattern | Use for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Short verify / ad-hoc chat** | Lead-in sentence, then `<blockquote><p>One imperative sentence.</p></blockquote>` | Channel list checks, single draft requests, rewrite-one-network asks. Public posts show a hover **Copy** button on each blockquote. SSR adds `id="blog-prompt-N"` and JSON-LD `CreativeWork` (`learningResourceType`: agent prompt) via `BlogPosting.hasPart`. |
| **Shell on the Bot computer** | `<pre><code>npm install …</code></pre>` plain text, no escaped HTML inside | `openquok` install, curl skill fetch |
| **Long routine / foundation prompts** | `<pre><code>…</code></pre>` multi-line plain text | House rules, daily scan, weekly fill, viral watch—anything the reader pastes into Grok Bot or saves as a routine |

**Do not** put multi-paragraph routine prompts inside `<blockquote>` with `<br>` chains—copy is awkward and layout is hard to read. **Do not** wrap prompt text in escaped HTML inside `<pre><code>` (no `&lt;p&gt;` soup); the blog pipeline may unwrap it, but plain text is the source of truth.

When a post compares length to competitor articles, count **non-prompt prose** separately: strip `<pre><code>…</code></pre>` (and optional blockquote verify lines) before word-count targets.

## Internal links (pass equity)

Use **root-relative** paths. The normalizer strips `rel`/`target` on same-site and `/…` hrefs so they stay **dofollow**. Do not add `rel="nofollow"` on internal anchors.

Also link `/docs/…`, `/playbooks`, `/channels/{slug}` when those pages match the sentence. Channel slugs follow the channel catalog (`channels/index.ts`; `tiktok`, `instagram`, …).

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD — Skill Builder is the destination; hub is not a substitute -->
<p>Assemble <code>openquok-core</code> in <a href="/tools/skill-builder">Skill Builder</a> instead of zipping by hand.</p>
<p>For TikTok recipes, start from the <a href="/tools/skill-builder/tiktok">TikTok Skill Builder</a>.</p>

<!-- ❌ BAD — generic hub when the post is about skills -->
<p>See our <a href="/tools">free tools</a>.</p>
```

Absolute `https://www.openquok.com/…` is treated as internal (followable). Prefer `/tools/skill-builder` (and siblings) so self-host and preview stay same-origin in the editor.

## External links

Third-party `http(s)` get `rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"` + `target="_blank"` on display. You do not need to hand-author those attributes.

## SERP pass (optional)

Before a long Feature Walkthrough or competitive keyword post, run `.cursor/skills/serp-analysis/` (upstream [serp-analysis](https://github.com/aaron-he-zhu/aaron-marketing-skills/tree/main/seo-geo/survey/serp-analysis)) and store the brief + copy-paste fields under `docs/blog/*-blog-manager-copy-paste.md` (see `docs/blog/browser-extension-walkthrough-blog-manager-copy-paste.md`).

## Checklist (blog HTML)

- [ ] Primary tool link is the matching page (`/tools/skill-builder` for skill posts) — not only `/tools`
- [ ] Channel tool URLs use catalog slugs when a platform is named
- [ ] Headings stay `h2` / `h3` (TipTap); no extra `h1` in the body
- [ ] Comparison grids use HTML `<table>` (Visual toolbar **Insert table**, or paste `<table>` in HTML source then switch to Visual) — the editor schema keeps table markup; public posts wrap tables for horizontal scroll and emit Schema.org `Table` JSON-LD (`#blog-table-N`)
- [ ] FAQ answers and How-to steps can include the same internal `<a href="/tools/skill-builder">` links (admin Visual / HTML source)
- [ ] FAQ / HowTo stay in the admin SEO fields, not copied into `content`
- [ ] **Audience card** filled when the post targets a clear persona (recommended for how-tos); title + description in admin only—not duplicated in `content`
- [ ] **Agent prompts**: short asks in `<blockquote><p>…</p></blockquote>`; long paste/routine text in `<pre><code>…</code></pre>` (not blockquotes full of `<br>`)
